Table full name: bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.txt
Column name: submission_number Type: STRING Description: Accession Number. The 20-character string formed from the 18-digit number assigned by the Commission to each EDGAR submission. submission_number: [adsh]
Column name: measure_tag Type: STRING Description: The unique identifier (name) for a tag in a specific taxonomy release. measure_tag: [tag]
Column name: version Type: STRING Description: For a standard tag, an identifier for the taxonomy; otherwise the accession number where the tag was defined. For example, \"invest/2013\" indicates that the tag is defined in the 2013 INVEST taxonomy.
Column name: period_end_date Type: INT64 Description: The end date for the data value, rounded to the nearest month end. period_end_date:[ddate]
Column name: num_quarters Type: INT64 Description: The count of the number of quarters represented by the data value, rounded to the nearest whole number. A point in time value is represented by 0. num_quarters:[qtrs]
Column name: iprx Type: INT64 Description: A positive integer to distinguish different reported facts that otherwise would have the same primary key. For most purposes, data with iprx greater than 1 are not needed. The priority for the fact based on higher precision, closeness of the end date to a month end, and closeness of the duration to a multiple of three months. See fields dcml, durp and datp below.
Column name: language Type: STRING Description: The ISO language code of the fact content. language:[lang]
Column name: language_decimal Type: INT64 Description: The value of the fact \"xml:lang\" attribute, en-US represented by 32767, other \"en\" dialects having lower values, and other languages lower still. language_decimal: [dcml]
Column name: duration_fraction Type: FLOAT64 Description: The difference between the reported fact duration and the quarter duration (qtrs), expressed as a fraction of 1. For example, a fact with duration of 120 days rounded to a 91-day quarter has a durp value of 29/91 = +0.3187. duration_fraction: [durp]
Column name: date_fraction Type: FLOAT64 Description: The difference between the reported fact date and the month-end rounded date (ddate), expressed as a fraction of 1. For example, a fact reported for 29/Dec, with ddate rounded to 31/Dec, has a datp value of minus 2/31 = -0.0645. date_fraction: [datp]
Column name: dimension_hash Type: STRING Description: The 32-byte hexadecimal key for the dimensional information in the DIM data set. dimension_hash: [dimh]
Column name: num_dimensions Type: INT64 Description: Small integer representing the number of dimensions, useful for sorting. Note that this value is function of the dimension segments. num_dimensions: [dimn]
Column name: coregistrant Type: STRING Description: If specified, indicates a specific co-registrant, the parent company, or other entity (e.g., guarantor). NULL indicates the consolidated entity. Note that this value is a function of the dimension segments. coregistrant: [coreg]
Column name: escaped Type: BOOL Description: Flag indicating whether the value has had tags removed.
Column name: source_length Type: INT64 Description: Number of bytes in the original, unprocessed value. Zero indicates a NULL value. source_length: [srclen]
Column name: text_length Type: INT64 Description: The original length of the whitespace normalized value, which may have been greater than 8192. text_length: [txtlen]
Column name: footnote Type: STRING Description: The plain text of any superscripted footnotes on the value, as shown on the page, truncated to 512 characters, or if there is no footnote, then this field will be blank.
Column name: footnote_length Type: INT64 Description: Number of bytes in the plain text of the footnote prior to truncation. footnote_length: [footlen]
Column name: context Type: STRING Description: The value of the contextRef attribute in the source XBRL document, which can be used to recover the original HTML tagging if desired.
Column name: value Type: STRING Description: The value, with all whitespace normalized, that is, all sequences of line feeds, carriage returns, tabs, non-breaking spaces, and spaces having been collapsed to a single space, and no leading or trailing spaces. Escaped XML that appears in EDGAR \"Text Block\" tags is processed to remove all mark-up (comments, processing instructions, elements, attributes). The value is truncated to a maximum number of bytes. The resulting text is not intended for end user display but only for text analysis applications.
Column name: _PARTITIONTIME Type: TIMESTAMP
