Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• quick_summary.submission_number – primary key to link with submission table  
• quick_summary.measure_tag – allows us to keep only revenue–type facts ('Revenues','SalesRevenueNet','SalesRevenueGoodsNet')  
• quick_summary.value – monetary amount we will aggregate (divide by 1 000 000 000 to express in billions)  
• quick_summary.units – keep only amounts expressed in ‘USD’  
• quick_summary.number_of_quarters (qtrs) – keep rows where qtrs = 4 (full‑year data)  
• quick_summary.fiscal_year – filter to fiscal_year = 2016  
• submission.submission_number – join key to quick_summary  
• submission.stprba – U.S. state/province of the registrant’s business address; used for grouping; exclude NULL or ''  
• submission.countryba – keep only rows where countryba = 'US' (optional extra filter)  

Typical conditions  
• WHERE measure_tag IN ('Revenues','SalesRevenueNet','SalesRevenueGoodsNet')  
• AND number_of_quarters = 4  
• AND fiscal_year = 2016  
• AND units = 'USD'  
• AND stprba IS NOT NULL AND stprba <> ''  

Below are ten exploratory–to–final BigQuery SQL statements (all SELECT‑only) you might run step‑by‑step; each shows 20 rows max.

```sql
-- 1️⃣ Description: Inspect distinct revenue‑related tags that actually appear in quick_summary.
SELECT DISTINCT measure_tag
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.quick_summary`
WHERE measure_tag IN ('Revenues','SalesRevenueNet','SalesRevenueGoodsNet')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2️⃣ Description: Peek at a few FY‑2016, 4‑quarter revenue facts (all units) before any joins.
SELECT submission_number, measure_tag, fiscal_year, number_of_quarters AS qtrs, units, value
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.quick_summary`
WHERE fiscal_year = 2016
  AND number_of_quarters = 4
  AND measure_tag IN ('Revenues','SalesRevenueNet','SalesRevenueGoodsNet')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3️⃣ Description: Join a sample of those facts to the submission table to see state codes.
SELECT qs.submission_number, s.stprba AS state, qs.units, qs.value
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.quick_summary` qs
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.submission`     s
  USING (submission_number)
WHERE qs.fiscal_year = 2016
  AND qs.number_of_quarters = 4
  AND qs.measure_tag IN ('Revenues','SalesRevenueNet','SalesRevenueGoodsNet')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4️⃣ Description: List distinct non‑blank U.S. state codes present in FY‑2016 data.
SELECT DISTINCT s.stprba
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.quick_summary` qs
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.submission` s USING (submission_number)
WHERE qs.fiscal_year = 2016
  AND qs.number_of_quarters = 4
  AND qs.measure_tag IN ('Revenues','SalesRevenueNet','SalesRevenueGoodsNet')
  AND s.stprba IS NOT NULL AND s.stprba <> ''
  AND s.countryba = 'US'
ORDER BY s.stprba
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5️⃣ Description: Check whether all revenue facts are in USD for our target subset.
SELECT units, COUNT(*) AS cnt
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.quick_summary` qs
WHERE fiscal_year = 2016
  AND number_of_quarters = 4
  AND measure_tag IN ('Revenues','SalesRevenueNet','SalesRevenueGoodsNet')
GROUP BY units
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6️⃣ Description: Sample of revenue values (converted to billions) with their states.
SELECT s.stprba AS state,
       qs.value/1e9 AS revenue_bil,
       qs.measure_tag
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.quick_summary` qs
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.submission` s USING (submission_number)
WHERE qs.fiscal_year = 2016
  AND qs.number_of_quarters = 4
  AND qs.measure_tag IN ('Revenues','SalesRevenueNet','SalesRevenueGoodsNet')
  AND qs.units = 'USD'
  AND s.stprba IS NOT NULL AND s.stprba <> ''
  AND s.countryba = 'US'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7️⃣ Description: Aggregate total FY‑2016 revenue (billions) by state, show top 20.
SELECT s.stprba AS state,
       ROUND(SUM(qs.value)/1e9, 2) AS total_revenue_bil
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.quick_summary` qs
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.submission` s USING (submission_number)
WHERE qs.fiscal_year = 2016
  AND qs.number_of_quarters = 4
  AND qs.measure_tag IN ('Revenues','SalesRevenueNet','SalesRevenueGoodsNet')
  AND qs.units = 'USD'
  AND s.stprba IS NOT NULL AND s.stprba <> ''
  AND s.countryba = 'US'
GROUP BY state
ORDER BY total_revenue_bil DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8️⃣ Description: Verify how many unique companies (submission_numbers) each top‑5 state has.
WITH rev AS (
  SELECT s.stprba AS state, qs.submission_number
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.quick_summary` qs
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.submission` s USING (submission_number)
  WHERE qs.fiscal_year = 2016
    AND qs.number_of_quarters = 4
    AND qs.measure_tag IN ('Revenues','SalesRevenueNet','SalesRevenueGoodsNet')
    AND qs.units = 'USD'
    AND s.stprba IS NOT NULL AND s.stprba <> ''
    AND s.countryba = 'US'
)
SELECT state, COUNT(DISTINCT submission_number) AS num_companies
FROM rev
GROUP BY state
ORDER BY num_companies DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9️⃣ Description: Show the single largest revenue figure within each of the top 10 revenue states.
WITH per_state AS (
  SELECT s.stprba AS state,
         qs.value/1e9 AS revenue_bil
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.quick_summary` qs
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.submission` s USING (submission_number)
  WHERE qs.fiscal_year = 2016
    AND qs.number_of_quarters = 4
    AND qs.measure_tag IN ('Revenues','SalesRevenueNet','SalesRevenueGoodsNet')
    AND qs.units = 'USD'
    AND s.stprba IS NOT NULL AND s.stprba <> ''
    AND s.countryba = 'US'
)
SELECT state,
       MAX(revenue_bil) AS biggest_single_company_revenue_bil
FROM per_state
GROUP BY state
ORDER BY biggest_single_company_revenue_bil DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 🔟 Description (FINAL): Identify the U.S. state with the highest total FY‑2016 revenue in billions.
SELECT s.stprba AS state,
       ROUND(SUM(qs.value)/1e9, 2) AS total_revenue_bil
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.quick_summary` qs
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.sec_quarterly_financials.submission` s USING (submission_number)
WHERE qs.fiscal_year = 2016
  AND qs.number_of_quarters = 4
  AND qs.measure_tag IN ('Revenues','SalesRevenueNet','SalesRevenueGoodsNet')
  AND qs.units = 'USD'
  AND s.stprba IS NOT NULL AND s.stprba <> ''
  AND s.countryba = 'US'
GROUP BY state
ORDER BY total_revenue_bil DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

